---
source: Secrets to Smoking on the Weber Smokey Mountain Cooker and Other Smokers
author: Bill Gillespie
serves: 4
cook time: 5 minutes
---

In a #small bowl{}, whisk @olive oil{1/2%cup}, @balsamic vinegar{1/4%cup}, @agave{2%Tbsp}, and @fresh cracked pepper{1/2%tsp} together for the vinaigrette. Store in the #refrigerator{} until ready to use.

Fire up the #grill{} to 400°F and higher (or Weber Smokey Mountain cooker set up for direct grilling, one zone).

Lightly drizzle the cut side of @romaine lettuce{2%heads} (washed and halved lengthwise) with @olive oil{}, then season with @salt{} and @pepper{} to taste.

When grilling the romaine lettuce, the grill should be 400°F and higher. Place the romaine halves onto the grill cut side down. Grill checking the underside frequently until a nice char forms, about 1 to ~{2%minutes}. Flip and grill the other side for 1 to ~{2%minutes}.

Remove from the grill and sprinkle @freshly grated Parmesan cheese{1/2%cup} over each half on the cut side, then drizzle with the balsamic vinaigrette. Alternatively, chop the grilled lettuce, transfer to a #large bowl{}, and toss with the Parmesan cheese and balsamic vinaigrette before serving.
